 "contract": "Facet input contract, one rule set for the Python and Rust encoders and for both preflight tools. numeric: integers within (-2^53, 2^53), integral floats, booleans as 0 and 1 (compatibility), strings that are an integer literal with an optional sign; fractional numbers, other strings, and non scalar values are rejected; null is missing. boolean: booleans, and numbers exactly 0 or 1 (compatibility); anything else is rejected; null is missing. categorical: strings only; null is missing. Legacy symbol() keeps truncation of fractional numbers and truthiness on boolean fields for compatibility; the checked encoders and preflight apply this contract.",
 "flow": "---\nname: input_contract\nstart: assess\n---\n\n## assess\n-> page: when error_rate >= 25\n-> ticket: when error_rate >= 5\n-> watch: when user_facing\n-> hold: when region == \"eu\"\n-> done: else\n\n## page\n\n## ticket\n\n## watch\n\n## hold\n\n## done\n",
